00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:04.270
Minami? You seem different today.

00:14:04.870 --> 00:14:05.780
Did anything happen?

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:07.650
Just a whim.

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:09.300
You're lying!

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:10.550
Something definitely happened!

00:14:10.550 --> 00:14:11.620
There's something weird!

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:12.430
How rude!

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:16.060
Keiko! What happened to your glasses?

00:14:16.060 --> 00:14:19.720
I'm trying out contacts, but they're a bit painful.

00:14:19.720 --> 00:14:21.460
I'm thinking about just taking them off.

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:23.720
So you're doing things on a whim too!

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:24.610
You're weird!

00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:25.170
Weird?!

00:14:27.900 --> 00:14:29.220
Kiko, are you having a whim-sy day too?

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:32.850
My hair wouldn't stay down this morning so I just tied it-

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:34.050
Fujioka-kun?!

00:14:34.950 --> 00:14:35.820
You're weird!

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:36.430
Weird?!

00:14:38.380 --> 00:14:39.770
Everyone's different today...

00:14:40.210 --> 00:14:41.240
What is going on?!

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:44.160
I guess whims doesn't always mean good.

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:45.190
What is going on?!
I guess whims doesn't always mean good.

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:45.520
What is going on?!

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:49.820
What was I feeling at that point?

00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:52.880
I wasn't feeling bad that morning.

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:55.280
If anything, I was feeling absolutely great.

00:14:55.280 --> 00:14:58.580
Yes. I should have been feeling exceptionally great.

00:14:59.130 --> 00:15:02.370
Hosaka, you look like something's wrong. Did anything happen?

00:15:02.370 --> 00:15:04.210
Then again, you always look like something's wrong.

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:09.340
I made salad the other day on a whim, but I can't remember its taste!

00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:06.660
I like mayonnaise.

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:10.110
I can't remember!

00:16:10.730 --> 00:16:14.750
Was it salad oil? Olive oil? Did I put salt in it?

00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:16.580
Are you sure it was a salad?
Did I just hold it all in my mouth?

00:16:19.600 --> 00:16:22.120
Yeah. If I were to use a metaphor,

00:16:23.190 --> 00:16:27.090
the salad was like the glimpse of
an illusionary world shown to me by God.

00:16:28.010 --> 00:16:28.630
I got it!

00:16:29.320 --> 00:16:34.080
I'll name that salad
"Hosaka's Salad of Illusionary Delights Made on a Whim"!

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:35.890
If you can't remake it, why don't you just forget about it?

00:16:36.450 --> 00:16:41.210
Today's lunch is fried rice made on a whim with leftovers.

00:16:41.210 --> 00:16:42.640
Do you remember how to make it?

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:45.650
Minami-ke!

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:57.490
You took another shower?

00:16:58.050 --> 00:16:59.920
Well, it's hot today.

00:16:59.920 --> 00:17:04.500
If you like showering that much, why don't you just wear a bathing suit?

00:17:05.950 --> 00:17:09.290
Yeah, then I wouldn't even have to change- Hey!

00:17:26.010 --> 00:17:28.080
Chiaki, let's go to the pool!

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:29.470
Welcome.

00:17:29.470 --> 00:17:31.230
There's already someone all ready to swim!

00:17:31.670 --> 00:17:34.990
Um, are you going to the pool too, Kana-chan?

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:37.940
Eh? But that takes effort...

00:17:37.940 --> 00:17:39.630
She's not ready to swim!

00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:41.100
Well then, let's go, Chiaki!

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:43.040
Didn't you say you wanted to practice the crawl stroke?

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:45.500
Eh, I'll pass.

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:48.840
Just trying to get there would be too hot.

00:17:48.840 --> 00:17:51.040
No one was ready to swim!

00:17:52.600 --> 00:17:55.870
Too bad. I was so excited to go that I wore my swimsuit underneath.

00:17:55.870 --> 00:17:56.540
Right?

00:17:57.220 --> 00:17:58.170
Right!

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:00.740
Just strip down to your swimsuits already!

00:18:00.740 --> 00:18:02.900
How long are you planning on making me be the only one in a swimsuit?

00:18:02.900 --> 00:18:03.930
It's embarrassing!

00:18:04.380 --> 00:18:06.820
So why are you in a swimsuit, Kana-chan?

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:12.220
Air conditioner!

00:18:15.590 --> 00:18:18.200
Getting down to just your swimsuit is pretty refreshing.

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:19.570
Yeah.

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:21.100
But it's still too hot!

00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:22.640
Yeah.

00:18:22.640 --> 00:18:26.640
Huh? Chiaki's found a fan while we weren't looking!

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:28.330
That's not fair!

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:29.600
Not fair?

00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:34.080
Don't you understand just how logical this is?

00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:34.830
What?

00:18:35.430 --> 00:18:39.640
I'm the one wearing the most clothes. Therefore, I am the hottest.

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:42.060
Therefore, it's only logical that I have the fan!

00:18:42.060 --> 00:18:43.930
It's so unfair I don't even understand.

00:18:44.380 --> 00:18:46.170
I'll give you this.

00:18:46.940 --> 00:18:47.890
A fan?

00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:50.910
We only have one.

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:51.640
Well...

00:18:51.640 --> 00:18:54.590
I guess we can have one person fan the rest.

00:18:59.850 --> 00:19:03.780
Then let's have Chiaki, who's being cooled by the electric fan, fan us!

00:19:13.350 --> 00:19:14.880
I can't do this. Good night.

00:19:15.680 --> 00:19:16.550
Already?!

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:18.500
Yes. I'm already done and I'm tired.

00:19:19.290 --> 00:19:21.680
I can't believe she can fall asleep in this heat.

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:23.290
I guess she's just that tired.

00:19:23.290 --> 00:19:23.930
I got it!

00:19:24.650 --> 00:19:27.180
If you work hard and use the fan, you'll get tired.

00:19:27.840 --> 00:19:30.430
You'll be able to fall asleep from being tired!

00:19:32.570 --> 00:19:33.190
Good night.

00:19:34.960 --> 00:19:35.940
Good night.

00:19:38.680 --> 00:19:41.940
Why don't I get anyone to fan?!

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:44.450
I'm right here in the dream. Probably.

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:45.420
Mako-chan... Heh, you're so...
I'm right here in the dream. Probably.

00:19:45.420 --> 00:19:47.070
I wonder why... but then again...
Mako-chan... Heh, you're so...

00:19:47.070 --> 00:19:47.950
I wonder why... but then again...

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:50.200
Oh, this is refreshing too!

00:19:50.840 --> 00:19:51.950
But this isn't it.

00:19:52.360 --> 00:19:55.330
Awawa, zhisss izzz refrreshshing.

00:19:55.830 --> 00:19:57.000
No, this isn't it.

00:19:57.620 --> 00:20:00.970
Kana-chan, Chiaki, Yoshino, wake up!

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:03.500
I want to fan someone too!

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:04.860
I'm home.

00:20:07.220 --> 00:20:08.800
Haruka-chan, welcome home!

00:20:09.130 --> 00:20:11.930
I bet it was really hot outside. I'll fan you!

00:20:11.930 --> 00:20:13.810
Oh... Thank you.

00:20:14.200 --> 00:20:15.890
All right. Time to sleep.

00:20:18.170 --> 00:20:21.250
Wait, tell me why everyone's in a swimsuit before you fall asleep!

00:20:21.250 --> 00:20:23.780
That's...

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:26.400
Why is everyone in their swimsuit?!

00:21:59.320 --> 00:22:03.300
...and there's the flan from that store and donuts from that other store!

00:22:03.300 --> 00:22:04.950
That store's great, isn't it?

00:22:05.820 --> 00:22:08.260
Why didn't you call us over?

00:22:08.960 --> 00:22:11.750
<i>Maki... there's a piece of rice on your mouth.</i>

00:22:12.410 --> 00:22:14.710
<i>What should I do? Should I tell her?</i>

00:22:15.510 --> 00:22:15.970
All right.

00:22:16.510 --> 00:22:17.190
Hey...

00:22:17.190 --> 00:22:18.310
What is it, Natsuko?

00:22:18.310 --> 00:22:20.900
You've been looking at me like you want to say something.

00:22:21.450 --> 00:22:24.400
Well, if it's about how beautiful I am, I supposed that's totally natural.

00:22:24.870 --> 00:22:27.070
Don't stare at me too much. It's embarrassing.

00:22:27.470 --> 00:22:28.940
Yeah...

00:22:28.940 --> 00:22:30.220
Anyway, what's up?

00:22:30.820 --> 00:22:31.730
It's nothing.

00:22:32.800 --> 00:22:34.450
<i>This is rather difficult.</i>

00:22:34.800 --> 00:22:37.120
Oh, I just realized but...

00:22:37.830 --> 00:22:39.040
<i>Did Haruka notice as well?</i>

00:22:39.400 --> 00:22:41.940
Maki, you somehow look like a rice ball!

00:22:41.940 --> 00:22:43.860
What does that mean? Does it mean I'm beautiful?

00:22:44.890 --> 00:22:48.500
<i>Does that mean she's noticed the piece of rice?</i>

00:22:48.960 --> 00:22:52.090
It's more like Akitamochi-brand rice rather than Koshihikari rice.

00:22:52.090 --> 00:22:53.380
Does that mean I'm an early bloomer or something?

00:22:54.120 --> 00:22:57.930
<i>So does having rice on her face make her look like a rice ball?</i>

00:22:58.360 --> 00:22:59.680
'Sup.

00:22:59.680 --> 00:23:00.570
Hitomi!

00:23:00.570 --> 00:23:02.640
Did you girls have lunch already?

00:23:02.640 --> 00:23:04.560
I came hoping to get some food.

00:23:04.560 --> 00:23:06.690
We've got nothing left. Go home.

00:23:07.040 --> 00:23:09.440
You know, Senpai, your face looks round today.

00:23:09.980 --> 00:23:11.820
What does that mean? That I'm beautiful?

00:23:12.260 --> 00:23:13.400
How should I say this...?

00:23:13.400 --> 00:23:16.370
You look kind of like a rice ball today.

00:23:16.740 --> 00:23:18.690
Yeah, she looks like a rice ball, doesn't she?

00:23:18.690 --> 00:23:21.560
Is the seaweed crispy or soft?

00:23:22.420 --> 00:23:24.340
A bit on the soft side today.

00:23:24.340 --> 00:23:26.330
Maybe moisturizers were a good call?

00:23:27.220 --> 00:23:29.880
<i>So do they realize there's a piece of rice on her...?</i>

00:23:30.390 --> 00:23:31.130
Yo.

00:23:31.530 --> 00:23:32.960
Hey, Hayami-senpai!

00:23:32.960 --> 00:23:35.540
We don't have any leftovers for you to take.

00:23:35.540 --> 00:23:36.890
Oh, you don't?

00:23:37.910 --> 00:23:42.840
Maki, you make me want to take you on a picnic.

00:23:42.840 --> 00:23:44.310
I'm not a rice ball, you know.

00:23:44.710 --> 00:23:46.100
Are you a pickled plum?

00:23:46.100 --> 00:23:47.470
Or could you be salmon?

00:23:47.470 --> 00:23:49.240
I'm not a rice ball.

00:23:50.420 --> 00:23:52.780
Man, why's everyone acting so weird today?

00:23:53.310 --> 00:23:55.790
<i>All right. I've got to tell her now.</i>

00:23:56.720 --> 00:23:57.000
Ma-

00:23:57.000 --> 00:23:57.450
Maki.
Ma-

00:23:58.840 --> 00:24:00.790
H-Hosaka-senpai?

00:24:03.720 --> 00:24:06.210
What do you think is the ultimate lunch?

00:24:06.850 --> 00:24:07.760
With seaweed?

00:24:08.370 --> 00:24:09.590
Or a Nakonochi lunch?

00:24:11.490 --> 00:24:13.840
<i>I guess you just can't help taking your shirt off...</i>

00:24:14.510 --> 00:24:17.890
Um, this question is pretty sudden...

00:24:18.320 --> 00:24:19.740
I see, Rice Balls.

00:24:19.740 --> 00:24:21.730
That is not my name!

00:24:21.730 --> 00:24:23.140
You mean that your name isn't Rice Balls?

00:24:23.600 --> 00:24:26.970
If your name isn't Rice Balls... then who are you?

00:24:27.440 --> 00:24:28.190
My name is Maki!!

00:24:29.360 --> 00:24:31.050
So Rice Balls was Maki...

00:24:31.760 --> 00:24:33.440
Or perhaps Maki was Rice Balls?

00:24:33.950 --> 00:24:35.310
That is the question.

00:24:36.390 --> 00:24:37.350
What is up with everyone today?!

00:24:37.350 --> 00:24:38.990
There is no question.
What is up with everyone today?!

00:24:46.570 --> 00:24:47.750
<i>It came off!</i>

00:24:49.170 --> 00:24:51.880
It's fine. Everything will be okay.

00:24:52.890 --> 00:24:54.260
Maki!

00:24:58.950 --> 00:25:02.010
After seeing you, I'm getting an urge for takoyaki.

00:25:02.010 --> 00:25:03.560
Does that mean I'm beautiful?

00:25:03.870 --> 00:25:05.950
<i>So she's normally a takoyaki?</i>
